{"id":"id-1792326342550","object":"chat.completion","created":1792326342,"model":"@cf/openai/gpt-oss-120b","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"R-b Verdikt: C — Begründung: Der aktuelle Zustand lässt N nur als pending‑Zeile bestehen, weil kein Parser‑Arm für skalare Referenzkonstanten existiert. Ein lokaler, nicht lizenzierter Ansatz vermeidet weitere Komplexität, bis die Direktiven implementiert werden. — Riss: phi/sources.phi fehlt ein Arm für skalare Referenzkonstanten, wodurch keine Registrierung möglich ist.\n\nR-f Verdikt: A — Begründung: Das Teilmodell D=2190 (999 MB) ist offiziell und bleibt innerhalb akzeptabler Speichergrenzen. Es vermeidet die Inkonsistenzen großer Dateien und die Notwendigkeit eines Epoch‑Parameters. — Riss: Das Abstract gibt 5399 Seiten an, während die Datei‑Tail‑Größe 5480 Seiten beträgt – ein klarer Widerspruch.\n\nR-g Verdikt: B — Begründung: Der Parser‑Fix für kg/(m² s) und die Stern‑Metadaten‑Achse decken die kritischsten Anwendungsfälle ab, ohne die Architektur zu überfrachten. Weitere Restgruppen können später modular ergänzt werden. — Riss: Ohne FDSN‑Key‑Aufspaltung lässt sich der BHZ‑Kanal nicht korrekt zuordnen, was zu Datenverlust führt.","refusal":null,"annotations":null,"audio":null,"function_call":null,"reasoning":"We need to answer three open questions, each in a specific format:\n\n`R-<x> Verdikt: <A|B|C|D> — Begründung: <zwei Sätze> — Riss: <stärkster Gegenbeleg oder ungemessene Größe>`\n\nWe have three sections: R-b, R-f, R-g. For each we need to pick one of the options (A, B, C, D) and give a brief justification in exactly two sentences. Then \"Riss\" should be the strongest counter-evidence or unmeasured size.\n\nWe must not invent facts. So we need to base on the given info. Provide concise answer.\n\nWe must not add extra text beyond the required format for each question. Probably each answer on its own line.\n\nLet's craft:\n\nR-b: Options A, B, C, D. Need decide. The issue: phi/sources.phi missing arm, N stays None. Options: A new directives ellipsoid + normal_gravity (Parser-Arm). B own constant block with url/terms. C local-only, N pending. D only future gfc-block, a/f/omega/gamma0 remain unregistered. Additional: N stays pending as pending line or absence? Likely best is to keep N pending as a line to indicate missing value, not absent. Option C says local-only, N remains pending. That matches. So choose C.\n\nR-f: Options A D=2190 (official part model), B Cap 3211, C full D=5540 (split/R2), D D=760 or Cap 719. Need decide. Considering size constraints: D=2190 is 999 MB, acceptable, official part model. Probably best to choose A.\n\nR-g: Options A all arms (largest), B smallest safe subset (kg/(m^2 s)-parser fix + star metadata axis), C nothing, D each rest own form. Need decide minimal needed: parser fix + star metadata axis likely sufficient. So choose B.\n\nNow need Riss: strongest counter-evidence or unmeasured size.\n\nR-b: strongest counter-evidence: the missing arm for scalar reference constants makes any new directive ineffective because parser cannot handle them; also N stays None. So Riss could be \"phi/sources.phi ohne Arm verhindert Registrierung aller Konstanten\". Or \"Unmessbare Größe: fehlende scalar reference constant\". Provide.\n\nR-f: strongest counter-evidence: the abstract says size 5399 but file tail indicates 5480, causing mismatch; also compiler refuses without epoch. So Riss: \"Inkonsistenz zwischen Abstract (5399) und Dateigröße (5480)\". Or \"Kein Epoch-Parameter verfügbar\". Choose one.\n\nR-g: strongest counter-evidence: missing quantity/channel arm for many groups, especially FDSN-BHZ key parsing fails, so minimal subset may still break other groups. So Riss: \"Fehlender FDSN-Key-Parser verhindert korrekte Zuordnung von BHZ-Kanälen\". Provide.\n\nMake sure each line exactly matches format: `R-b Verdikt: C — Begründung: ... — Riss: ...`\n\nTwo sentences in Begründung. Ensure German, concise.\n\nLet's craft.\n\n","reasoning_content":"We need to answer three open questions, each in a specific format:\n\n`R-<x> Verdikt: <A|B|C|D> — Begründung: <zwei Sätze> — Riss: <stärkster Gegenbeleg oder ungemessene Größe>`\n\nWe have three sections: R-b, R-f, R-g. For each we need to pick one of the options (A, B, C, D) and give a brief justification in exactly two sentences. Then \"Riss\" should be the strongest counter-evidence or unmeasured size.\n\nWe must not invent facts. So we need to base on the given info. Provide concise answer.\n\nWe must not add extra text beyond the required format for each question. Probably each answer on its own line.\n\nLet's craft:\n\nR-b: Options A, B, C, D. Need decide. The issue: phi/sources.phi missing arm, N stays None. Options: A new directives ellipsoid + normal_gravity (Parser-Arm). B own constant block with url/terms. C local-only, N pending. D only future gfc-block, a/f/omega/gamma0 remain unregistered. Additional: N stays pending as pending line or absence? Likely best is to keep N pending as a line to indicate missing value, not absent. Option C says local-only, N remains pending. That matches. So choose C.\n\nR-f: Options A D=2190 (official part model), B Cap 3211, C full D=5540 (split/R2), D D=760 or Cap 719. Need decide. Considering size constraints: D=2190 is 999 MB, acceptable, official part model. Probably best to choose A.\n\nR-g: Options A all arms (largest), B smallest safe subset (kg/(m^2 s)-parser fix + star metadata axis), C nothing, D each rest own form. Need decide minimal needed: parser fix + star metadata axis likely sufficient. So choose B.\n\nNow need Riss: strongest counter-evidence or unmeasured size.\n\nR-b: strongest counter-evidence: the missing arm for scalar reference constants makes any new directive ineffective because parser cannot handle them; also N stays None. So Riss could be \"phi/sources.phi ohne Arm verhindert Registrierung aller Konstanten\". Or \"Unmessbare Größe: fehlende scalar reference constant\". Provide.\n\nR-f: strongest counter-evidence: the abstract says size 5399 but file tail indicates 5480, causing mismatch; also compiler refuses without epoch. So Riss: \"Inkonsistenz zwischen Abstract (5399) und Dateigröße (5480)\". Or \"Kein Epoch-Parameter verfügbar\". Choose one.\n\nR-g: strongest counter-evidence: missing quantity/channel arm for many groups, especially FDSN-BHZ key parsing fails, so minimal subset may still break other groups. So Riss: \"Fehlender FDSN-Key-Parser verhindert korrekte Zuordnung von BHZ-Kanälen\". Provide.\n\nMake sure each line exactly matches format: `R-b Verdikt: C — Begründung: ... — Riss: ...`\n\nTwo sentences in Begründung. Ensure German, concise.\n\nLet's craft.\n\n"},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop","stop_reason":null,"token_ids":null,"routed_experts":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":834,"completion_tokens":961,"total_tokens":1795,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"neurons":92.05891418457031}}